# NetGen - Batch Neural Network Model Generator

Generate N model training folders with verified parameter counts in a target range.

## Quick Start

```bash
# Generate 50 ML models with 10K-100K params
python netgen.py --range 10000-20000 --count 20 --output ./my_models

# Generate big models
python netgen.py --range 500000-1000000 --count 10 --output ./big_models

# Command format
python netgen.py --range <range> --count <count> --output <file path>

```

## Each Generated Folder

```
001-mlp-200x150x80/
├── model.py      # Model definition (PyTorch nn.Module)
├── data.py       # Synthetic dataset (SynData class)
├── train.py      # Training script (CE loss, Adam)
├── eval.py       # Evaluation script
├── config.py     # Hyperparameters
└── README.md     # Documentation
```

## Run a Model

```bash
cd 001-mlp-200x150x80
python train.py
python eval.py
```

## Supported Architectures

- **MLP**: Multi-layer Perceptron
- **Deep MLP** (`deep`): Many hidden layers (same width) — scales as N×d²
- **Wide Net** (`wide`): One huge hidden layer — scales as d_in×d_hidden
- **LSTM**: Long Short-Term Memory
- **GRU**: Gated Recurrent Unit
- **CNN**: Convolutional Neural Network (8×8 images)
- **AE**: Autoencoder
- **Stacked AE** (`sae`): Deep autoencoder with multiple encoder/decoder layers
- **VAE**: Variational Autoencoder
- **Transformer** (`tf`): Transformer encoder stack — scales as L×d_model²
- **Linear**: Single linear layer (regression)

**Range coverage**: 2 params (Linear(1,1)) to 10¹²+ params (Deep with 100K×100 layers).
For huge ranges (>100M), deep/wide/transformer architectures are preferred automatically.
